# Styles: rules in a separate styles file (09-separate-file.styles.stxt), and the document winning over it.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Styles · A separate styles file
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		# The same name as in the styles file: the document wins, also in the rules of the file.
		Named color: house #6B2A5E
	Section:
		Text: Styles
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: A separate styles file
		Paragraph: The rules can live in a document of their own, with `Styles` as its root, passed along when converting. This document has none of the rules it uses: they are in `09-separate-file.styles.stxt`, beside it. Its own `Styles` declares the color `house` again, and the document wins: the panel of the file comes out plum instead of green.
			Style: intro
		Text: Style: panel, from the styles file, with Named color: house from the document
			Style: label
		Paragraph: The rules shared by many documents go in one file, and each document keeps only its content.
			Style: panel
		Text: Style: tag, from the styles file
			Style: label
		Text: Shared rule
			Style: tag
